     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily ibuprofen dose for adults. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rise substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some possible intended orders:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day), which is typical for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg four times daily. The order may have mixed up the per-dose and daily amounts.\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg per dose, please confirm that it's intentional and give the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
